        "path": "/data/corpora/cloudflare-state-v1/files/workflows/get-started/guide.md",
        "text": "   You can pass a [retry configuration](/workflows/build/sleeping-and-retrying/) to `step.do()` to customize how failures are handled. See the [full step API](/workflows/build/workers-api/#step) for stream requirements, limits, and additional methods like `sleepUntil` and `waitForEvent`.\n\n   When deciding whether to break code into separate steps, ask yourself: \"Do I want all of this code to run again if just one part fails?\" Separate steps are ideal for operations like calling external APIs, querying databases, or reading files from storage - if a later step fails, your Workflow can retry from that point using data already fetched, avoiding redundant API calls or database queries.\n\n",
        "rank": 1,
        "score": 0.5870048999786377,
